[Term]
id: GO:0140358
name: P-type transmembrane transporter activity
namespace: molecular_function
def: "Primary active transporter that auto-phosphorylates (hence P) at a key conserved aspartate residue, generating a conformational change that allows transport of the substrate. Hydrolysis of the phosphorylated Asp residue, catalyzed by the actuator (A) domain, results in another state with occluded substrates. Upon dissociation of Mg2+ and Pi, the enzyme reverts to the initial state, in which the counter-transported substrate is released into the cytosol." [PMID:18075584, PMID:25918123]
synonym: "E1-E2 ATPase" EXACT [Wikipedia:P-type_ATPase]
